<title>SINGAPORE: Taiwan raises fuel oil bunker price by $3/tonne.</title>
<headline>Taiwan raises fuel oil bunker price by $3/tonne.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's Chinese Petroleum Corp (CPC) has raised its spot and term prices of bunker fuel effective September 18, a company statement said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Posted prices for 180-, 280- and 380-centistoke bunker fuel delivered at the ports of Keelung, Hualien, Taichung and Suao were increased by $3 per tonne, at $141 per tonne. Term prices were also raised by $3, at $138.</p>
<p>Spot and term bunker C grade was also up by $3, at $139 and $136 respectively.</p>
<p>CPC is state owned and the country's sole supplier of bunker fuels. --Singapore Newsroom (+65-8703080)</p>
</text>
